## Evaluation ownership

{{EVALUATION_TABLE}}

- The task evaluator runner creates raw evidence; its owner checks the pass condition.
- The harness evaluator compares baseline, control, and treatment effects without reusing the task verdict.
- Record repeated failures, cost, cold-start, and parity incidents in rolling state; the checker returns `none|targeted|full`.
- The improvement owner proposes a change only after full evidence identifies a harness cause or the user makes an evidence-backed request. The request path must establish baseline and full evidence before applying a candidate.

## Runtime projections

